% =====================================================================
% DETROIT MUGETSU - ABC NOTATION (hook melody + piano riff + chant)
% Single-song package for MUGETSU-GUMI (the Moonless Company)
% =====================================================================
% The hook melody below is an ORIGINAL DESK COMPOSITION, composed
% by the desk for the filed hook lyric - built to the hook's rhythm
% and verdict weight. It is a composition draft under the Flagpole,
% not a transcription of any recording.
% Production spec (from the strike prompt pack): Detroit bounce
% trap, 144 BPM, G# minor (desk key choice: the song's family spine
% is the Unfriendly Ghost album's 144 BPM / G# minor seat, and the
% Brightmoor Signature's home pack - Album III - rides G# minor).
% Key signature G# minor: F, C, G and D sound sharp.
% Chords use the G# minor family: G#m (i), E (VI), C#m (iv),
% D# (V).
% Lyrics: gangsta-brief.txt in this folder (HOOK + VERSE 1 filed
% text; VERSES 2-3 + OUTRO desk drafts) - folded byte-exact into
% DETROIT-MUGETSU-PROMPT.md.
% Flagpole of Claim and Coinage: Johnathan 'Qasparr' Monroe,
% ARR, All Rights Reserved, Without Prejudice.
% =====================================================================

X:1
T:Detroit Mugetsu
C:Desk composition for the hook lyric (draft)
M:4/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=144
K:G#m
%%score 1 2
%% Formation: KUROGANE verses (body) - YAMI SUNG hook (low alto,
%% the hook as verdict) - SHION outro chant (see X:2).
%% V:1 = the hook melody: a low declaration out of Brightmoor,
%% rising to the dominant on the moonless-sky line, falling home
%% dark, and landing the crown line on a held tonic -
%% "a crown isn't stolen, it's worn."
%% V:2 = the Brightmoor Signature piano riff: the four-note motif
%% G# - E - D# - B opens every bar IDENTICALLY (the signature),
%% the grand-piano arpeggio fills around the bar's chord.
%% Hook lyric: "Detoroito umare, Buraitomuua sodachi..."
V:1
"G#m"G B d d B G B2|"E"e2 e d B c B2|"C#m"c c c B c e c2|"D#"d d f f g f d2|
"G#m"g f d B d B G2|"E"e e e d c d e2|"C#m"G B c d e d c2|"D#"f f d B "G#m"B2 G2|]
V:2
G/2 E/2 D/2 B,/2 G/2 B/2 d/2 B/2 G/2 E/2 D/2 B,/2 G/2 B/2 d/2 g/2|
G/2 E/2 D/2 B,/2 E/2 G/2 B/2 e/2 G/2 E/2 D/2 B,/2 E/2 G/2 B/2 e/2|
G/2 E/2 D/2 B,/2 C/2 E/2 G/2 c/2 G/2 E/2 D/2 B,/2 C/2 E/2 c/2 G/2|
G/2 E/2 D/2 B,/2 D/2 F/2 A/2 d/2 G/2 E/2 D/2 B,/2 D/2 F/2 d/2 A/2|
G/2 E/2 D/2 B,/2 G/2 B/2 d/2 B/2 G/2 E/2 D/2 B,/2 G/2 B/2 d/2 b/2|
G/2 E/2 D/2 B,/2 E/2 G/2 B/2 e/2 G/2 E/2 D/2 B,/2 B/2 e/2 g/2 e/2|
G/2 E/2 D/2 B,/2 C/2 E/2 G/2 c/2 e/2 c/2 G/2 E/2 C/2 E/2 G/2 c/2|
G/2 E/2 D/2 B,/2 D/2 F/2 A/2 d/2 f/2 d/2 A/2 F/2 G/2 B/2 d/2 G/2|]

X:2
T:Detroit Mugetsu - Outro (The Invocation)
C:Desk composition for the chant (draft)
M:4/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=60
K:G#m
%% SHION alone, slow chant over silence: the four invocation
%% lines of the trance-aid brief, one bar each, long tones in
%% the moonless key. Drums out under the last line; one 808
%% hit; hard stop.
%% Chant: "Akuma no mai, Mugetsu. / Bitto Bankai wa sanmai
%% nari. / Murasaki no honoo wa moyasazu, iyasu. / Tsuki
%% naki sora ni mau."
"G#m"G4 B4|"G#m"d4 B4|"E"e4 d4|"G#m"B4 G4|]
